  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KORE3408</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Korean 8</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This unit follows on from KORE3407 Korean 7. It further enhances students' linguistic skills in Korean and their cultural literacy, develops their ability to critique contemporary social and cultural issues in Korean, and equips them with effective expressions and communication techniques via the complex linguistic structures and vocabulary used in contemporary Korean spoken and written discourses. 
Students develop their skills in:
-speaking and listening, by means of a research project presentation, discussion, and development of competence in academic registers in spoken language; and 
-reading and writing, by means of essay writing in academic format, critical reading of Korean journal articles, and Korean-to-English translation.
Successful completion of this unit aims to bring students to the equivalent of Level 4/Level 5 of the Test of Proficiency in Korean (TOPIK).
This unit also facilitates future pathways into higher research on Korea through promoting critical selection and utilisation of Korean language source materials.</hasUnitDescription>
  <hasCreditPoints rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</hasCreditPoints>
  <hasPrerequisiteText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Successful completion of KORE3407 Korean 7</hasPrerequisiteText>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

