  <hasUnitAssessment rdf:resource="#assessment9"/>
  <hasUnitAssessment rdf:resource="#assessment71"/>
  <hasUnitAssessment rdf:resource="#assessment329"/>
  <hasContactRequirement rdf:resource="#contactrequirement1"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome2067"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome2072"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome2069"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome2071"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome2070"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome2068"/>
  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">IREL1001</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The International Politics of Climate Change</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This unit introduces students to the international politics of climate change. The unit first looks briefly at theories of environmental politics, using concepts from international relations and environmental politics, to introduce students to debates on how we should think about the planet and its politics. It then looks at key actors that participate in climate politics, including states, intergovernmental organisations, transnational corporations and social movements, and how these actors clash to produce political and environmental outcomes. Its case studies include the United Nations process for dealing with climate change, and key environmental regions such as the Himalayan watershed, the Arctic and Antarctic, and the Amazon rainforest. The unit also takes students through key contemporary issues such as borders and frontiers in the contemporary world, and the positive and negative impact of technology on the climate. Students are introduced to the politics of climate change, why it is so hard to deal with, and begin to think through what political solutions to environmental problems might look like.</hasUnitDescription>
  <hasCreditPoints rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</hasCreditPoints>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

