  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SSEH3552</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Coaching and Athlete Development</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This unit focuses on coaching, training programming, and athlete development, offering students a comprehensive understanding of the coach's role in maximising athlete potential. Through an integrated approach of sports science disciplines, students gain an understanding of coaching strategies of relevance for high performance settings.
By analysing a variety of sports and scenarios, students will explore all aspects of coaching including key psychological aspects of athlete development, creating tailored training plans, and implementing skill acquisition strategies. Through an interdisciplinary approach, this unit equips students with the knowledge and skills needed to excel as coaches in competitive sports and other high-performance environments.</hasUnitDescription>
  <hasCreditPoints rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</hasCreditPoints>
  <hasPrerequisiteText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Successful completion of SSEH2240 Motor Learning and Control or  Enrolment in CM017 Bachelor of Sport and Exercise Sciences and Master of Public Health or CM018 Bachelor of Sport and Exercise Sciences and Master of Clinical Exercise Physiology or CM019 Bachelor of Sport and Exercise Sciences and Master of Applied Human Performance Science</hasPrerequisiteText>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

