  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome3092"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome3091"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome3086"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome3090"/>
  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome3085"/>
  <isInMajor rdf:resource="#MJD-PHYGY"/>
  <hasPrerequisite rdf:resource="#PHYL1001"/>
  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PHYL3003</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Nutritional and Metabolic Physiology</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This Level 3 unit comprises a series of lecture, laboratory, and tutorial sessions. Each session helps a student to understand the importance of qualitative and quantitative aspects of nutrition for basic sustenance as well as growth and activity. Normal function is supplemented with activities that investigate scenarios when various pathologies lead to metabolic dysfunction. The unit covers the function and regulation of the gastrointestinal system by examining the digestion an absorption of macro- and micronutrients. Energy balance in the body and disorders that result in impaired metabolic function are evaluated. The unit builds on the material covered in Level 1 PHYL1001 Physiology – how your body works. The unit further develops student's laboratory techniques for physiological measurement, focusing on data recording, statistical analysis, and the graphical presentation of data. The unit has a major focus on written scientific communication. The results from two of the laboratories are used to complete two scientific papers. The unit also reinforces aspects of teamwork and interpersonal skills in both experimental work and communication.</hasUnitDescription>
  <hasCreditPoints rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</hasCreditPoints>
  <hasPrerequisiteText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Successful completion of PHYL1001 Physiology - How your body works and 96 points or Successful completion of 48 points and  Enrolment in MJD-IMSCP Integrated Medical Sciences and Clinical Practice</hasPrerequisiteText>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

