  <hasOutcome rdf:resource="#outcome3442"/>
  <hasLocation rdf:resource="#Albany"/>
  <hasPrerequisite rdf:resource="#MGMX1135"/>
  <hasPrerequisite rdf:resource="#MGMX1136"/>
  <hasPrerequisite rdf:resource="#MGMT1136"/>
  <hasPrerequisite rdf:resource="#MGMT1135"/>
  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MGMT2302</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Leadership</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This unit helps students to develop the knowledge and skills required to understand leadership and be an effective leader. These two goals are achieved in parallel by taking students through a five-part series of the leadership process
1. What is leadership and how can you develop it? 
2. What do you bring to your role as leader? 
3. What is your style and who do you lead?
4. What do you do when you lead?
5. Special topics on leadership 
The unit involves learning and application of theories via evidence-based approaches; and in parallel offers the opportunity for students to develop skills in reflection, self-awareness and self-regulation in relation to their own leader development goals. Learning activities include lectures, readings, case-study videos; and a tutorial series that incorporates a variety of activities in including, self-assessment, experiential learning, individual reflection and group discussion.</hasUnitDescription>
  <hasCreditPoints rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</hasCreditPoints>
  <hasPrerequisiteText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Successful completion of MGMT1135 Organisational Behaviour or MGMX1135 Organisational Behaviour or MGMT1136 Management and Organisations or MGMX1136 Management and Organisations</hasPrerequisiteText>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

