  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MKTG2238</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Marketing communications</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Marketing communications is one of the most prominent areas of marketing. There are many opportunities and issues in the fast-paced world of communications, which includes advertising, promotions, sponsorship, events, and public relations among others. This unit will cover all the areas of marketing communications across all types of organisations and industries, giving you a foundation for potential work in this field. You will learn how to assess and critique communications from organisations, and the strategy behind them. You will also have the opportunity to develop your own communications campaigns.</hasUnitDescription>
  <hasCreditPoints rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</hasCreditPoints>
  <hasPrerequisiteText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MKTG1203 Introduction to Marketing or MKTX1203 Introduction to Marketing</hasPrerequisiteText>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

