  <hasUnitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MKTG3305</hasUnitCode>
  <hasUnitTitle rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Marketing for Social Purpose</hasUnitTitle>
  <hasUnitLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</hasUnitLevel>
  <hasUnitDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Social marketing applies marketing principles to influence behaviours that benefit individuals and society, addressing critical issues such as public health, environmental sustainability, and social justice. But how do we craft campaigns that effectively inspire positive behaviour change? This unit will answer that question, immersing students in real-world social marketing challenges and strategies. Students will explore how to identify target behaviours, segment audiences, and develop compelling value propositions that resonate with diverse groups. Additionally, students will learn how to design, implement, and evaluate social marketing campaigns, equipping you with the strategic and creative tools necessary to tackle societal issues and drive meaningful change</hasUnitDescription>
  <hasCreditPoints rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</hasCreditPoints>
  <hasPrerequisiteText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Successful completion of MKTG1203 Introduction to Marketing</hasPrerequisiteText>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

